@@ -101,6 +101,26 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send web push notifications to people's phones and desktops, so whatever lands in their notifications tray also reaches their devices.
+Each person turns them on for the device they're using from their notification settings.
+
+To enable this, generate a VAPID key pair:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm fizzy bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}", "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Then set both keys when running Fizzy:
+
+```sh
+docker run --env VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=... --env VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=... ...
+```
+
+Keep the same key pair once people have subscribed: changing it means everyone has to turn push notifications on again.
+Browsers only allow push notifications on sites served over HTTPS.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
